<newsitem itemid="171034" id="root" date="1996-11-06" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: UPF lifts year pretax profits 19 pct.</title>
<headline>UPF lifts year pretax profits 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year to August 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		12.05		  vs 10.06</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 2.9		    vs 2.75</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 4.5		    vs 4.25</p>
<p> Pretax		     6.7		    vs 5.7</p>
<p> Turnover		   55.4		   vs 47.8</p>
<p>NOTE - UPF Group Plc, a UK manufacturer of pressings and fabrications for the car and consumer goods sectors, said the year had started well, that it saw a further rise in value for investors and would continue to examine growth opportunities.  </p>
<p> Operating profit	 7.48		   vs 6.01</p>
<p> Interest charge	  0.88		   vs 0.37</p>
<p> Tax			  1.32		   vs 0.40</p>
<p> Profit for the year    5.42		   vs 5.28</p>
<p> Retained profit	  3.01		   vs 3.67</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 17, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  Nov 26</p>
<p> Ex-div date		Nov 18</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
